## Initial Engineering Approach

The first CORR-002 implementation used fixed 10-minute buckets:

```spl
| bin _time span=10m
```

This approach was rejected because events that occurred only a few minutes apart could fall into different fixed buckets.

Example:

```text
4:09 PM — Remote Network Logon
4:11 PM — PowerShell
```

Although the events are only two minutes apart, a fixed bucket boundary could prevent correlation.

---

## Diagnostic Investigation

A temporary diagnostic query was used to confirm that both event types existed and were being classified correctly.

The diagnostic demonstrated that Splunk could identify the relevant activity types, but fixed-window grouping and overly restrictive PowerShell filtering were preventing reliable correlation.

This led to a redesigned correlation strategy.

---

## Final Correlation Strategy

The final implementation uses chronological event processing.

For each PowerShell event, Splunk identifies the most recent preceding remote network logon on the same host.

The actual elapsed time between the events is then calculated.

Conceptually:

```text
Remote Network Logon
        |
        v
Store Logon Timestamp
        |
        v
PowerShell Event
        |
        v
Find Most Recent Prior Logon
        |
        v
Calculate Time Difference
        |
        v
<= 600 Seconds?
     /       \
   NO         YES
   |           |
Ignore      CORR-002
```

---

## Final CORR-002 SPL

```spl
index=* ((EventCode=4624 AND LogonType=3) OR EventCode=4104)
| where EventCode=4104 OR (EventCode=4624 AND IpAddress!="-" AND IpAddress!="127.0.0.1" AND IpAddress!="::1")
| eval activity=case(EventCode=4624,"network_logon",EventCode=4104,"powershell")
| eval network_time=if(activity="network_logon",_time,null())
| eval network_account=if(activity="network_logon",TargetUserName,null())
| eval network_ip=if(activity="network_logon",IpAddress,null())
| sort 0 host _time
| streamstats last(network_time) as prior_network_time last(network_account) as prior_account last(network_ip) as prior_source_ip by host
| where activity="powershell"
| eval time_difference=_time-prior_network_time
| where isnotnull(prior_network_time) AND time_difference>=0 AND time_difference<=600
| eval correlation="CORR-002 - Remote Network Logon Followed by PowerShell"
| eval risk=65
| eval severity="HIGH"
| eval powershell_time=_time
| convert ctime(prior_network_time) ctime(powershell_time)
| table host correlation severity risk prior_network_time powershell_time time_difference prior_account prior_source_ip
```

